Slythe wrote:

> And someone must tell me what the dump-patch is....

It's a patch that dumps lots of data about your character when the game 
ends (by death, ascension, or otherwise). If you compile your own game, 
you can find the patch for the sources on 
<http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html>. I think there's also a 
precompiled version for most major platforms, but I don't know where. It 
does save a lot of copy-pasting in case of an ascension...

> Anyway, now that i've done a straight ascension, can someone direct me
> to a page where the various conducts are explained? I'm curious to
> know what extinctionist is, and how can one ascertain that conduct?

An extinctionist is someone who has a very high boredom threshold, I've 
heard. It's not checked by the game, so the definitions of when one has 
succeeded differ. See 
<http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/extinctionist-faq.html> for 
extinctionist information, and 
<http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/conduct.html> for information on the 
conducts the game keeps track of.

